## Architecture

Paths below are relative to the Godot project (game/ by default):

```
content/  data: weapons, enemies, encounters, movement and sound/VFX definitions
domain/   engine-free rules: health, ammo, cooldowns, resources, states, seeded RNG
input/    commands shared by human controls, recorded input and scenario bots
world/    Godot physics, movement, collision queries, navigation, scene lifecycle
render/   meshes, animation, cameras, weapon viewmodel, VFX and positional audio
ui/       HUD, menus and settings; emits commands, displays actual state
tests/    pure-rule suites/replay and scenarios exercising the production paths
```

domain/ extends RefCounted; no Node, Input, Time or unseeded RNG. Fixed ticks and
stable iteration. World physics belongs in world/ and is tested with documented
tolerances. A pure-rules hash says nothing about whole-world physics determinism.
Rendering does not own damage or cooldowns. Bots do not get a second movement or
combat implementation. Networking, if selected, follows the frozen network module.

