## Tools and gates

Use Bash on every OS. GODOT_BIN and BLENDER_BIN pin executables; GP_PYTHON selects
Python 3. Record exact version strings in pipeline/toolchain.json after doctor;
both tools are checked against those pins on production runs. GP_PROJECT_DIR
selects the Godot root; --project overrides it. Logs live in out/gp-runs/.

```
bash {{AGENT_DIR}}/scripts/{{PREFIX}}-doctor.sh
bash {{AGENT_DIR}}/scripts/{{PREFIX}}-fps-godot.sh --init-harness
bash {{AGENT_DIR}}/scripts/{{PREFIX}}-runner-godot.sh
bash {{AGENT_DIR}}/scripts/{{PREFIX}}-sim-godot.sh --replay --seed 4242
bash {{AGENT_DIR}}/scripts/{{PREFIX}}-fps-godot.sh --all
bash {{AGENT_DIR}}/scripts/{{PREFIX}}-mesh-build.sh --spec art/prompts/<id>.json
bash {{AGENT_DIR}}/scripts/{{PREFIX}}-mesh-validate.sh --all
bash {{AGENT_DIR}}/scripts/{{PREFIX}}-style-lock.sh --verify
bash {{AGENT_DIR}}/scripts/{{PREFIX}}-runner-godot.sh --export --out build/game/game.exe
```

Each gate emits one JSON line. Read pass; zero exit alone is not a pass. Missing
dependencies/harnesses, invalid evidence and timeouts are distinct error_kind
results. Gate success never implies subjective visual or control quality.
Export needs Windows export templates and the real main-scene QA bridge.

## Art and evidence

Style: art/style/style-bible.json, frozen stylized-3d profile and references.
Recipes: tools/blender/. Mesh specs: art/prompts/. Production records: art/builds/.
GLBs: game/assets/models/ with sibling .provenance.json. Commit production
records with assets; they bind recipe, dependencies, tool version, reference
sheet, profile, frozen spec and exact output bytes. No production before STYLE
LOCK. Generated images need image-register.sh provenance. Reimport GLBs through
wrapper scenes and verify actual collision, animation and material behavior.
Blockouts are allowed to test gameplay; they do not satisfy final art requirements.

Keep STATE.md current; append decisions/history to DOCUMENTATION.md. Code board:
{{AGENT_DIR}}/specs/. Art board: art/cards/. Memory at {{MEMORY_PATH}} is append-only.
Never delete files; archive superseded work. No paired model experiment protocol.
